-- title:
--   Homogeneity and coefficient positivity of the rank-weight polynomial
-- statement:
--   Let $E$ be a finite set of size $d$, $N$ a matroid on $E$, and $r_N(A)$ the finite natural-number rank of $A\subseteq E$. Introduce a fresh homogenizing variable $z_0$, distinct from the variables $z_a$ for $a\in E$, and define $$P_{N,q}(z_0,z)=\sum_{A\subseteq E}(q^{r_N(A)})^{-1}z_0^{d-|A|}\prod_{a\in A}z_a.$$ For rational $q>0$, $$P_{N,q}\text{ is homogeneous of degree }d,\qquad [z^m]P_{N,q}\ge0\quad\text{for every exponent vector }m.$$ The exponent vectors range over the homogenizer and all label coordinates.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/meelgroup/counting-matroid/blob/dd16a4628fdb095c58fe0f3dfd8e353c6e97443c/CountingMatroid/Analysis/RankWeightCoordinateLorentzian.lean#L25-L76

